From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:19:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: snps,dwc3-common: Add
 snps,inv-sync-hdr-quirk

Bit 30 of the DWC_usb31 LLUCTL register makes the link layer detect Gen2
receiver polarity from the data block sync header. On the Allwinner A733
some Gen2 devices link at Gen1 unless it is set. Add a quirk property for
it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the property is
accepted on the controller node and read back in the device tree
(snps,inv-sync-hdr-quirk present).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml          | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
index 6c0b8b653824..35f2d0949871 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/snps,dwc3-common.yaml
@@ -207,6 +207,13 @@ properties:
       avoid -EPROTO errors with usbhid on some devices (Hikey 970).
     type: boolean
 
+  snps,inv-sync-hdr-quirk:
+    description:
+      When set, the link layer detects Gen2 receiver polarity from the data
+      block sync header (DWC_usb31 LLUCTL bit 30). Without it some Gen2
+      devices link at Gen1 on Allwinner A733.
+    type: boolean
+
   snps,gfladj-refclk-lpm-sel-quirk:
     description:
       When set, run the SOF/ITP counter based on ref_clk.
